# One line per program in tests/corpus: its name, the exit status of
# the program built by rcc, and that of the program built by clang -O2.
# A status is a number up to 128, the name kill -l gives the signal a
# run died of, SEGV for SIGSEGV, or timeout for a run stopped at the
# time limit.  The shell reports a run that signal n killed as 128 + n,
# and timeout(1) gives 124 for a run it stopped, so no program exits
# above 128 or with 124 by itself, and no row holds a number above 128.
# A row with timeout in either column is long: tests/oracle runs its
# programs only when given --long, as make test-long gives it, and
# diffs and assembles the program on every run.
